🎤 47. Interview Questions

Q1. What is an anchor element?

Answer:

The "<a>" element is used to create hyperlinks in HTML.

---

Q2. What is "href"?

Answer:

"href" specifies the destination or reference of a hyperlink.

---

Q3. What is an external link?

Answer:

A link that points to another website or domain is called an external link.

Example:

<a href="https://github.com">
    GitHub
</a>

---

Q4. What is an internal link?

Answer:

A link that points to another page or location within the same website/project.

Example:

<a href="about.html">
    About
</a>

---

Q5. What is a relative path?

Answer:

A path that describes a file location relative to the current document.

Example:

images/profile.jpg

---

Q6. What is an absolute URL?

Answer:

An absolute URL contains the complete web address.

Example:

https://github.com

---

Q7. What is "target="_blank""?

Answer:

It requests that the link be opened in a new browsing context, commonly a new tab.

---

Q8. What is "rel"?

Answer:

"rel" describes the relationship between the current document and the linked resource.

---

Q9. What is "mailto:"?

Answer:

"mailto:" is used to create an email link.

Example:

<a href="mailto:example@gmail.com">
    Email
</a>

---

Q10. What is "tel:"?

Answer:

"tel:" is used to create a telephone link.

Example:

<a href="tel:+911234567890">
    Call
</a>

---

Q11. What is the "<img>" element?

Answer:

The "<img>" element is used to display images on a webpage.

---

Q12. What is "src"?

Answer:

"src" specifies the source/location of an image or other resource.

---

Q13. What is "alt"?

Answer:

"alt" provides alternative text for an image and is important for accessibility.

---

Q14. Does "<img>" have a closing tag?

Answer:

No. "<img>" is a void element.

---

Q15. What is an HTML attribute?

Answer:

An attribute provides additional information about an HTML element.

Example:

<a href="https://github.com">

Here:

href

is an attribute.

---

Q16. What is "id"?

Answer:

"id" identifies a particular element and should normally be unique within the page.

---

Q17. What is "class"?

Answer:

"class" assigns an element to one or more groups/classes and can be shared by multiple elements.

---

Q18. What is "<br>"?

Answer:

"<br>" creates a line break.

---

Q19. What is "<hr>"?

Answer:

"<hr>" represents a thematic break.

---

Q20. What is a void element?

Answer:

A void element does not have a normal closing tag.

Examples:

<img>
<br>
<hr>
<input>

