- Absolute URLs contain complete web addresses.
- "../" means one parent directory level.
- "target="_blank"" requests a new browsing context.
- "rel" describes the relationship with the linked resource.
- "mailto:" creates email links.
- "tel:" creates telephone links.
- Page-section links can use "#id".
- "<img>" displays images.
- "src" specifies the image source.
- "alt" provides alternative image text.
- Images can be stored in separate folders.
- Images can be made clickable by placing them inside "<a>".
- HTML attributes provide additional information.
- "id" identifies an element.
- "class" groups elements.
- "title" can provide additional information.
- "style" allows inline CSS.
- "download" can request download behavior.
- "<br>" creates a line break.
- "<hr>" represents a thematic break.
- Void elements do not have normal closing tags.
- Accessibility should be considered while creating webpages.

